dated_at":"2025-02-24T10:26:53Z","body":"@Calinou: after looking at that PR, I must say it does not satisfy my requirements.  \r\nI have a generic controller called \"Wireless Gamepad F710\" which follows the playstation layout, for which no name check would match, and no scheme would be returned. Therefore, I won't know about the joypad's abilities.  \r\nBut let's take a more interesting case: say I had one xbox controller with paddles, and one xbox controller without. The other PR wouldn't help me learn _which buttons the joypad actually has/supports_ (i.e. which has paddles?).  \r\n\r\nMoreover, relying on the device name is not reliable at all (depending on the OS/driver, you get different names for the same device), though I still see value in the other PR in the sense that it helps me localizing the button/axes names, provided all the constant strings are visibly documented outside the codebase.\r\n\r\nIn that sense, I'd say the two PRs actually harmonize with each other.\r\n\r\n_EDIT_: Just to give a bit more context, I also want to provide several joypad button/axes to action default mappings, then auto-select the most fitting one on first connect (and more supporting features)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677825342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2708759323","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100791#issuecomment-2708759323","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100791","id":2708759323,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hdGMb","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"http