ist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T18:54:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T18:54:42Z","body":"Fair enough. Though I would also use this code to give warnings if their connected joypad does not have some mandatory/preferred buttons/axes, e.g. has only one (or none) joystick and 2 are required (or preferred) - I know most have them, but some people like using retro controllers whenever possible.\r\n\r\nUntil this PR's future is decided I can do a custom build, keeping this change compatible is easy enough.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709016014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]